--- body ---
## Context
The author requests integration of three harnessing principles: keep scripts
dependency-free using standard Python where practical; document a manual route
that an agent can follow without running the script; and accept an explicit
"I cannot measure this" when evidence is insufficient. These reduce installation
failures, preserve useful procedures when automation is unavailable, and reduce
pressure to invent results.

## Scope
Integrate the principles into toolkit authoring guidance and demonstrate them on
one existing scripted workflow. Inventory existing guidance first, including
dependency management and diagnosis discipline; reconcile overlaps rather than
adding a parallel rule set. Prefer standard-library scripts, with justified
exceptions where a dependency materially improves reliability or capability.
State interpreter, system-tool, and service prerequisites honestly.

The manual route describes inputs, decisions, checks, and outputs without
requiring the helper script or newly written code. Keep one procedural
specification that automation implements; explain any limits or extra cost of
the manual route. Preserve authorization and verification requirements.

Measurement outputs distinguish measured, derived, estimated, and unavailable
results. An unavailable result states the missing evidence, what was attempted,
and what would permit measurement. Missing access or failed execution must not
be reported as zero, absence, or an all-clear.

## Relevant files
- rules/coding-python.md
- skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md
- skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md, if present; otherwise locate its maintained source
- rules/workflow.md (diagnosis discipline)
- One existing scripted skill and its helper, selected after inventory

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Record where each principle already exists and the remaining integration gaps.
- [ ] Update the maintained authoring guidance with the dependency default,
      justified exceptions, manual procedure, and explicit measurement limits;
      reconcile conflicts with existing environment rules.
- [ ] Apply the guidance to one existing scripted workflow and identify it in
      the implementation report; defer a toolkit-wide migration to separately
      scoped work if the inventory establishes a need.
- [ ] Demonstrate the selected workflow's manual route without its helper and
      compare its outcome with automation on the same known input.
- [ ] Demonstrate an unavailable-measurement case and a positive control,
      showing that missing evidence cannot produce a fabricated result or all-clear.
- [ ] Run checks appropriate to changed files; regenerate generated guidance
      or catalogs only when their sources change.

## Verification
Use a bounded procedural walkthrough and reproducible examples for the pilot.
Add behavioral tests only where script behavior changes; do not pin prose with
wording tests or introduce a new enforcement guard merely to police the principles.
This ticket authorizes integration work, not immediate replacement of every
existing dependency or a repository-wide rewrite.
